//// A host module called only from a module in a folder of the project —
//// `src/orm/entity.bp` calls `orm_host:table/1`, kept in
//// `src/sidecars/orm_host.erl` — is shipped and called on erlang and beam.
////
//// The gap this pins (`language-gaps.md` T16): the shipper read the first
//// segment of the module name `orm/entity` as a package name. A library root
//// that carries a package `orm` (here the cell's own `libs/orm/`, a root the
//// walk-up finds) was taken for the module's owner, its `src` was probed, and
//// the build was refused naming that package. The owner is the package the
//// build's module table gives the module: `orm/entity` is the project's.
////
//// commonJS and wasm refuse an `@External.Erlang`-only function
//// (`commonJS.expect`, `wasm.expect`).

pub mod orm;
import {orm.entity.describe};

pub fn main() {
    @print(describe("user"));
}
